{"id":"chatcmpl-4bf3851f-314d-4c23-940b-ff6bd94700dd","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246021,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When visual evidence is ambiguous (e.g., lateral views where laterality is hard to determine), the successful strategy was to triangulate across multiple independent expert models and a zoomed region-of-interest crop, then reconcile outputs against known anatomical priors. The final answer was chosen by combining model consensus with domain knowledge (normal right hemidiaphragm sits higher), rather than trusting any single model. This pattern generalizes to any task where a single view/model is insufficient to disambiguate a finding.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Triangulate ambiguous findings across multiple independent expert models before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Use a zoomed region-of-interest crop to directly inspect the specific anatomical area when model outputs conflict.\",\n    \"Reconcile conflicting model outputs against established domain priors (normal anatomy) to break ties.\",\n    \"Verify view/orientation metadata first, since laterality judgments depend on knowing the projection type.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Confirm view/orientation before assessing laterality; cross-check with multiple models; zoom into the region of interest; fall back on anatomical norms when models disagree.\",\n    \"Ambiguous visual classification\": \"When evidence is weak or conflicting, gather independent assessments, inspect the region directly at higher resolution, and use prior knowledge to arbitrate.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus tasks\": \"Treat each model as a noisy voter; seek agreement, and when disagreement persists, use domain constraints rather than majority vote alone.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the image view/orientation (e.g., frontal vs lateral) before assigning laterality.\",\n    \"Cross-validate the key finding with at least two independent sources and a direct zoomed inspection before finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":757,"total_tokens":1127,"completion_tokens":370,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":757},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":370}}}